# Guitar on a stand (issue 107): 1x1 tile, the old diagonal flipped over a horizontal line: the body sits north-east with its dark sound hole, the neck runs south-west to the headstock and tuners, as if the guitar stood on a stand facing into the room, with a small dusk tripod under the body. Shaded for light from the top-left (lit top and left edges, dark bottom and right). The first version (neck north-west, hanging) is in git history.
size: 16x16
